    skos:altLabel "information processing capability" ;
    skos:altLabel "organizational information capability" ;
    skos:altLabel "information conveyance capability" ;
    skos:definition "An information capability represents an organization's inherent capacity to transmit, process, and manage information content through established systems, protocols, or workflows. Analysts and IT professionals employ this term when assessing organizational readiness, designing information architectures, or evaluating data flow efficiency within corporate or institutional settings. The capability encompasses the structural and procedural elements that enable reliable information exchange, supporting decision-making, operational continuity, and strategic alignment. Used in organizational studies and information systems to describe an organization's inherent capacity to transmit, process, or manage information content effectively, often involving specific technologies, protocols, or workflows." ;
    skos:broader <https://signals.zndx.org/sdg#SDG_GENERIC> ;
    skos:inScheme <https://signals.zndx.org/sdg/scheme> .

<https://signals.zndx.org/sdg#SDG_ICE_FILLER_INFORMATIONITEM> a skos:Concept ;
