    skos:altLabel "Cross-Disciplinary Learning" ;
    skos:altLabel "Integrated Vocational Training" ;
    skos:definition "Interdisciplinary Education is an instructional process that integrates knowledge and methodologies from multiple academic disciplines. It combines content, methods, and perspectives from different fields to provide a comprehensive and cohesive learning experience. This approach fosters a deeper understanding of complex topics by connecting insights from various disciplines, enhancing the ability to address multifaceted challenges and develop integrated solutions. This term describes an instructional process that integrates knowledge and methodologies from multiple academic disciplines. It involves the combination of content, methods, and perspectives from different fields to provide a comprehensive and cohesive learning experience." ;
    skos:broader <https://signals.zndx.org/sdg#SDG_PROCESS> ;
    skos:inScheme <https://signals.zndx.org/sdg/scheme> .

<https://signals.zndx.org/sdg#SDG_PROCESS_FILLER_INVESTMENTCHOICEDECISION> a skos:Concept ;
