    skos:definition "A mathematical concept represents an abstract principle that underpins mathematical reasoning and quantitative analysis. These foundational ideas enable systematic problem-solving and support the development of algorithms and computational models. A mathematical concept represents an abstract principle that underpins mathematical reasoning and quantitative analysis. These foundational ideas enable systematic problem-solving and support the development of algorithms and computational models." ;
