    skos:altLabel "measurement dimension" ;
    skos:altLabel "physical measurement parameter" ;
    skos:altLabel "property quantifier" ;
    skos:definition "A measurement parameter specifies the exact physical property or dimension targeted during quantification, linking the abstract concept of a property to a concrete measurement unit. Practitioners employ this term when documenting experimental setups, calibration protocols, or data collection instruments that capture specific physical quantities. The parameter anchors the measurement process to a well-defined physical attribute, ensuring consistency across observations and repeatability in scientific reporting. Used in metrology and physical sciences to denote a specific property or dimension being measured, such as temperature, mass, or length, along with its associated unit and quantification method." ;
    skos:broader <https://signals.zndx.org/sdg#SDG_ICE_DESCRIPTIVE> ;
    skos:inScheme <https://signals.zndx.org/sdg/scheme> .

