    skos:altLabel "Analytical Calculation Program" ;
    skos:definition "The quantitative analytic tool functions as a research artifact designed specifically for performing numerical analysis and data interpretation. Practitioners utilize these tools to calculate statistical measures, process numerical datasets, and generate quantitative research outcomes. The instruments support systematic data examination procedures that require precise numerical computation and analytical processing capabilities. This term applies to instruments designed for performing numerical analysis and data interpretation within clinical or research settings." ;
    skos:broader <https://signals.zndx.org/sdg#SDG_MATERIAL_ENTITY> ;
