    skos:altLabel "historical Slavic root" ;
    skos:altLabel "Slavic language root" ;
    skos:definition "A Slavic linguistic root represents the foundational linguistic element from which specific Slavic languages and dialects evolve, preserving the historical continuity of vocabulary and grammatical structures. Researchers utilize this term when tracing etymological lineages, reconstructing proto-forms, or analyzing the historical development of Slavic language families. The root serves as the primary unit of comparison in comparative linguistics, enabling scholars to map phonological shifts and semantic changes across time. Applied in historical linguistics and philology to identify the ancestral linguistic forms or roots that serve as the foundation for the development of Slavic languages and their dialects." ;
    skos:broader <https://signals.zndx.org/sdg#SDG_ICE_DIRECTIVE> ;
    skos:inScheme <https://signals.zndx.org/sdg/scheme> .

