    skos:definition "An algorithm that learns from data patterns to make predictions. The model processes input data through learning mechanisms to identify patterns and generate outputs based on those learned patterns. This model applies when an algorithm learns from data patterns to generate predictions or classifications. The model operates in computational environments where training data feeds into learning processes that produce actionable outputs." ;
    skos:broader <https://signals.zndx.org/sdg#SDG_ICE_DIRECTIVE> ;
    skos:inScheme <https://signals.zndx.org/sdg/scheme> .

<https://signals.zndx.org/sdg#SDG_MATERIAL_ENTITY_FILLER_MAILDROPLOCATION> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "Filler Maildroplocation" ;
    skos:notation "2.2.56" ;
