    skos:definition "A regulatory body is a material entity that enforces a process regulation. This body ensures compliance with regulations and monitors regulatory adherence. The body operates within governance structures to enforce process regulations. A regulatory body is a material entity that enforces a process regulation. This body ensures compliance with regulations." ;
