    skos:definition "A research process that is conducted by a young researcher role. This term captures scientific investigations, data analysis, or experimental work actively performed by early-career researchers, such as doctoral candidates or postdoctoral fellows, often supported by mentorship or targeted funding programs. Applies to research processes actively conducted by young researchers, such as doctoral candidates or early-career scientists. Practitioners use this term when tracking research outputs, funding allocations, or mentorship initiatives focused on emerging scholars." ;
