    skos:definition "An Offline Channel is a dissemination channel that utilizes offline media. This channel includes television broadcasts, radio, and print. The channel reaches audiences through non-digital platforms. An Offline Channel is a dissemination channel that utilizes offline media. This channel includes television broadcasts, radio, and print. The channel reaches audiences through non-digital platforms." ;
